# Odyssey — always follow CLAUDE.md

Before doing any work in this repo, read and follow **`CLAUDE.md`** at the repo
root. It is the source of truth for this project's conventions and overrides any
default behavior. Key points (see CLAUDE.md for the full list):

- **Stack:** Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase + Prisma (via
  `src/lib/prisma/db.ts` only — never raw SQL), Clerk auth, Tailwind v4
  (no `tailwind.config.ts`), Leaflet (dynamic import, `ssr: false`).
- **Design tokens (ODY-012):** one system — CSS custom properties in the
  `:root` of `src/app/globals.css`, used via `var(--…)`. The legacy `odyssey-*`
  Tailwind aliases were removed — do not reintroduce them.
- **No inline styles** (Tailwind utilities or globals.css classes only). The
  only exception: truly dynamic per-element values passed as CSS custom
  properties, e.g. `style={{ "--f-color": color }}`, consumed by a class.
- **No hardcoded hex** outside globals.css.
- **No `localStorage` / `sessionStorage`.**
- **Server actions** live in `app/[route]/actions.ts`; **forms validate with
  Zod** (`src/lib/validations`) before the action; user sync via
  `getOrCreateUser()`.
- **DB schema changes:** use `prisma db push` (no migrations dir; Supabase
  free-tier auto-pauses).

## Working discipline

- Implement only what the current task asks; don't refactor unrelated code.
- When work is done, run the QA gate before considering it complete:
  `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npx tsc --noEmit`. Don't commit a failing gate.
- Never force-push, amend, skip hooks, merge, or open PRs unless explicitly told.
- If a task needs a decision or an action you can't safely perform, stop and ask
  rather than guessing.
